The failing test, in full, written before the routes exist:

```go
// AN UNCOMMITTED OBJECT MUST NOT BE REFERENCEABLE, AND THE POSITIVE HALF IS
// WHAT MAKES THIS LEG WORTH ANYTHING. v6's own note: a validator that rejects
// everything passes "an uncommitted asset is refused" perfectly, which is why
// the media routes come before the photo routes and why both halves are in
// one leg.
func TestAnAssetIsReferenceableOnlyAfterItIsCommitted(t *testing.T) {
	srv, bucket := newAPI(t) // real mux, real middleware, media.Memory
	token := registerAndSignIn(t, srv)

	png := media.FixtureHeroMountain // the bytes R1 captured
	sum := sha256.Sum256(png)
	digest := hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])

	// begin
	begun := postJSON(t, srv, token, "/v1/media", map[string]any{
		"sha256": digest, "byteSize": len(png), "contentType": "image/png",
	})
	if begun.Status != 201 {
		t.Fatalf("POST /v1/media = %d, want 201", begun.Status)
	}
	if begun.Body["id"] != digest {
		t.Errorf("id = %v, want the content hash %s — the address IS the digest",
			begun.Body["id"], digest)
	}
	if begun.Body["alreadyExists"] != false {
		t.Errorf("alreadyExists = %v on a first begin, want false", begun.Body["alreadyExists"])
	}

	// THE NEGATIVE: referencing it now must be refused, and by field name.
	before := putJSON(t, srv, token, "/v1/trips/kyoto", map[string]any{
		"name": "Kyoto in May", "coverAsset": digest,
	})
	if before.Status != 422 || before.Body["code"] != "invalid_field" || before.Body["field"] != "coverAsset" {
		t.Errorf("referencing an UNCOMMITTED object = %d %v, want 422 invalid_field on coverAsset",
			before.Status, before.Body)
	}

	// upload, then commit
	bucket.Put(t, digest, png)
	if c := postJSON(t, srv, token, "/v1/media/"+digest+"/commit", nil); c.Status != 200 {
		t.Fatalf("commit = %d, want 200", c.Status)
	}

	// THE POSITIVE: the same request now succeeds. Without this half the
	// negative above is satisfied by a validator that refuses everything.
	after := putJSON(t, srv, token, "/v1/trips/kyoto", map[string]any{
		"name": "Kyoto in May", "coverAsset": digest,
	})
	if after.Status != 200 {
		t.Fatalf("referencing a COMMITTED object = %d %v, want 200", after.Status, after.Body)
	}
	if after.Body["coverAsset"] != digest {
		t.Errorf("coverAsset = %v, want %s", after.Body["coverAsset"], digest)
	}
}
```

EXPECTED RED: `POST /v1/media = 404, want 201` — the mux's own 404, inside the JSON envelope, because httpx.MuxErrors already brings it there. That is the right reason. A red naming `undefined: media.FixtureHeroMountain` means R1 was skipped.

SECOND FAILING LEG, NEW AT v7.1 — the bounded conflict branch:

```go
// A client re-beginning an already-COMMITTED digest must not be able to
// restate what those bytes are. Executed by the database lens against the real
// table: without `WHERE media_objects.uploaded_at IS NULL` on the conflict
